      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i'm starting lifting for the first time and wanted to get into strength training. can u help me put together a basic 4 week linear progression program? mostly just want to focus on the big three like squat, bench, and deadlift to get a base.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A basic 4-week linear progression program for the big three is a solid start! You'll want to focus on consistent, steady increases in weight each week. For a beginner, starting with sets of 3-5 reps for your main lifts is usually best. Remember, the goal in these first few weeks is to build a solid foundation, not to go straight to maxing out, so don't be afraid to start with a weight you can handle comfortably.\n\nHere is a very simple template you can follow:\n\n**General Structure:**\n*   **Frequency:** Aim for 3 full-body lifting days per week (e.g., Monday, Wednesday, Friday).\n*   **Progression:** Each week, try to add a small amount of weight (like 2.5 lbs or 5 lbs) to the bar for your main lifts compared to the previous week.\n\n**Sample Weekly Breakdown:**\n\n| Week | Squat (Sets x Reps) | Bench Press (Sets x Reps) | Deadlift (Sets x Reps) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **1** | 3 x 5 | 3 x",
      "source": "target",
