    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. one more thing, i'm always worried about feeling too sore or just losing motivation when it gets hard. any tips for staying on track when i'm feeling unmotivated or just physically exhausted?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Feeling sore or losing motivation is completely normal when you start strength training! Don't let those feelings make you quit; that's when the real mental battle begins. When you're feeling unmotivated, just remember the small victories, like successfully completing a set or just showing up—that's a win in itself. If you feel physically exhausted, scale back instead of skipping entirely; maybe just do fewer sets or use lighter weights for a maintenance session.\n\nThink of your motivation like a small, stubborn fire that needs constant tending, not a giant roaring flame. Sometimes, the best way to rekindle that fire is to change your routine slightly, perhaps by trying a new warm-up or listening to some energetic music. Remember that consistency beats intensity when you're building a habit. You've got this!",
      "source": "target",
      "gen_token_ids": [
